# ScreenUtil design size

All responsive UI in this app scales against the design canvas defined in
`lib/core/common/app_config.dart` via `AppConfig.screenUtilDesignSize()`.

## Single source of truth

- **Design size lives in `AppConfig` only** — currently `Size(390, 844)` (logical phone canvas).
- **`ScreenUtilInit` must use it** — as in `lib/app.dart`:

```dart
ScreenUtilInit(
  designSize: AppConfig.screenUtilDesignSize(),
  builder: (context, _) { ... },
)
```

## Do / don't

```dart
// ❌ BAD — hardcoded design size in a widget, test, or second ScreenUtilInit
ScreenUtilInit(designSize: const Size(375, 812), ...);

// ❌ BAD — raw pixels instead of ScreenUtil extensions
padding: EdgeInsets.all(16),

// ✅ GOOD — rely on the global init + extensions
padding: EdgeInsets.all(16.w),
fontSize: 15.sp,
borderRadius: BorderRadius.circular(12.r),
16.verticalSpace,
```

## When changing the design canvas

1. Update **`AppConfig.screenUtilDesignSize()`** only (e.g. uncomment tablet
   branches when supporting tablets).
2. Do **not** duplicate `Size(...)` in other files.
3. Re-check layouts after a design-size change — `.sp`, `.w`, `.h`, and `.r`
   values scale relative to this canvas.

## Agent checklist for UI work

- [ ] No inline `designSize:` literals outside `AppConfig`
- [ ] Spacing/sizing uses `.sp` / `.w` / `.h` / `.r` / `.verticalSpace` /
      `.horizontalSpace`
- [ ] New `ScreenUtilInit` wrappers (tests, previews) call
      `AppConfig.screenUtilDesignSize()`
